#Application State
State of the application after implementing the articles and the most important learnings.

DaylyAI is an Android app (Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, minSdk 24) using MVVM with feature-based packages. Features: Articles (top headlines) and Sources (top-headlines/sources, country=us, category=business). Architecture: articles/data (ArticleData, ArticleApi, ArticleRepository, ArticlesResponse), articles/presentation (Article, ArticleUIState, ArticleViewModel), articles/ui (ArticleScreen, ArticleUIStateProvider); sources/data (SourceData, SourcesApi, SourcesRepository, SourcesResponse), sources/presentation (Source, SourceUIState, SourceViewModel), sources/ui (SourcesScreen, SourcesUIStateProvider). The di package holds shared Hilt wiring: NetworkModule provides Moshi, OkHttp (adds apiKey from BuildConfig.NEWS_API_KEY), Retrofit, ArticleApi, and SourcesApi. There is no per-feature network module (e.g. no SourcesNetworkModule). No domain layer. Stack: Hilt, Retrofit, Moshi, OkHttp, KSP (no kapt), StateFlow, Coil, Timber. Hilt is applied via the version catalog. Kotlin 2.3.10 and KSP 2.3.6 are used for compatibility with AGP 9 built-in Kotlin. DaylyAIApplication initializes Hilt and Timber; NEWS_API_KEY must be set in gradle.properties (injected on requests via OkHttp). Article.mapArticle() converts ArticleData into Article and formats dates as "Today", "Yesterday", or "X days ago". Source.mapSource() maps SourceData to Source (title from name).
Known issues and fixes
The Hilt Gradle plugin is published as com.google.dagger:hilt-android-gradle-plugin; resolving it with the usual plugin id from the catalog can fail. In that case, add it via the root buildscript (e.g. classpath("com.google.dagger:hilt-android-gradle-plugin:2.52")). Use plugin version 2.52 (not 2.52.1; that version does not exist). KSP 2.2.x used the kotlin.sourceSets DSL, which conflicts with AGP 9 built-in Kotlin and leads to "Using kotlin.sourceSets DSL to add Kotlin sources is not allowed" — upgrade KSP to 2.3.6 and Kotlin to 2.3.10. If build failures persist, ensure the app has INTERNET permission and that Timber is initialized in onCreate() of the Application class.
How to work effectively
Run ./gradlew assembleDebug after setting NEWS_API_KEY in gradle.properties. Keep presentation logic in presentation models; use Article.mapArticle() for mapping and formatting, not the ViewModel. Error messages shown to users are generic ("Something went wrong, please try again later"); technical errors should be logged with Timber.e(). For new features, keep data models, API interface, and repository under feature/data; add new Retrofit API bindings in di/NetworkModule (or extend di as needed) so networking stays centralized. MainActivity is @AndroidEntryPoint and shows MainScreen (bottom nav: Articles, Sources); ArticleViewModel and SourceViewModel are obtained via hiltViewModel() on each tab.
